Solve, algebraically.
\[
48\left({ }_{n} C_{4}\right)={ }_{(n+1)} P_{4}
\]

\section*{Solution}
\[
\begin{aligned}
48\left(\frac{n!}{(n-4)!4!}\right) & =\frac{(n+1)!}{((n+1)-4)!} \\
48\left(\frac{n!}{(n-4)!4!}\right) & =\frac{(n+1)!}{(n-3)!} \\
\frac{48}{4!} & =\frac{(n-4)!(n+1)!}{(n-3)!n!} \\
\frac{48}{24} & =\frac{(n-4)!(n+1)(n)!}{(n-3)(n-4)!(n)!} \\
2 & =\frac{n+1}{n-3} \\
2 n-6 & =n+1 \\
n & =7
\end{aligned}
\]

